'''{{PAGENAME}}''' ''(BBSL)'' is a virtual online version of ''Big Brother'' that took place during the 2006-2007 holiday season.

The season was made up of 15 different contestants that would have to interact in a virtual ''Big Brother House'' for at least 8 hours a day completing different tasks. After a few days, all of the contestants would decide who would stay and who would leave the house.

After 34 days, Madlen Flint, from Hungary, won the game and the prize of a virtual island that was valued at approximately US$ 1,675.
